; The width-less type names, refused. `Double` and `U8` here stand for
; the whole family (I8-I128, U8-U128, Isize/Usize, F32/F64): until
; 2026-08-14 each was an accepted name with no representational effect
; - a full-width i64, incompatible with Int - and the float spellings
; emitted INTEGER arithmetic on double bit patterns, silently, because
; the emitter keys float arithmetic on the name `Float` alone while
; the checker's tyIsFloatTy called these floats too.
; docs/memory-model.md MM-VAL-3c and MM-VAL-4b: "a conforming
; implementation MUST either give them widths or remove them." They
; are removed; the corpus population was zero.
(:: d (-> Double Double))

(fn (d x) x)

(:: u (-> U8 Int))

(fn (u x) 0)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
